ent-6991520465\n\nPR #92 remains a failed fixed pair: its ordinary child ran in a base Python 3.11 environment without Numba distribution metadata, and the validated-share child never started. This follow-up asks whether the unchanged root-local sharing candidate preserves the complete ordinary result and work under the pinned optional Python 3.11.17/NumPy 2.4.6/Numba 0.68.1/OpenSpiel 2.0.2 runtime.\n\nProtocol checkpoint `6f81e0096bfad473a83348a10a2e3b9395961bbc` preceded the source commit `0b9ae32b13959371952f8f853d5419d8708de8d1`. The latter adds a fail-closed runtime/license/old-evidence preflight and 12 focused tests. The three original candidate scripts, scientific-source fingerprint, fixed seeds, original loader/work checks and 180/900/1800/120-second caps are unchanged. The old own proof is carried forward only under exact source/input hashes.\n\nLocal exact-head source checks pass: both base roles 5,616 passed/72 skipped/150 deselected, Ruff, format and strict mypy (846 files); optional Python 3.11 2,522 passed; optional Python 3.12 2,521 passed/1 expected skip across 71 fixed suites; all-files hooks pass. Clean pre/post source guards confirm actual runtimes, 458-file scientific fingerprint and lock. A first optional Python 3.11 attempt was blocked before tests by a sandbox cache lock; its log is retained separately, and the identical suite passed with cache access. The protocol-only hosted CI passed both jobs. Hosted CI for the *source* commit is pending; source-check evidence is not yet published.\n\nNext: verify both hosted jobs on this exact source tree, publish the six-role source-check record and verify its public bytes, then reauthenticate the old public own proof and run one fixed complete optional-runtime pair. Raw pair evidence must be public before a data-only report and final checks. No pair has run on this branch. No CPU-saving, strategy or new admission claim is made. Earlier forecast, accuracy and full-context-copy failures remain failed.","l